  <processInformation>
    <dataSetInformation>
      <common:UUID>b00102ee-aba9-4097-9a59-32cb56a004ca</common:UUID>
      <name>
        <baseName xml:lang="en">Mixed C&amp;D waste, recycling, mobile plant</baseName>
      </name>
      <common:synonyms>Riciclo rifiuti C&amp;D in impianto mobile </common:synonyms>
      <classificationInformation>
        <common:classification name="ILCDCategories" classes="../ILCDClassification.xml">
          <common:class level="0">End-of-life treatment</common:class>
          <common:class level="1">Material recycling</common:class>
        </common:classification>
      </classificationInformation>
      <common:generalComment>Dataset developed within the ARCADIA project in the context of the Ph.D. of Federica Carollo (Politecnico di Milano). 
The dataset relates to recycling 1 tonne of mixed construction and demolition (C&amp;D) waste (EWC 17 09 04) in Italy.  
 
The dataset is composed of 9-unit processes:  
1) avoided the production of natural aggregates (For C1/C2 and C4 use) (Process: Inert natural mix from Lombardy Region);   
2) Water consumption for the waste treatment;  
3) Diesel consumption for the waste treatment; 
4) Steel-manganese alloy for mill jaws spare parts;  
5) Transport of ferrous metals to recovery (0.13% are a ferrous waste).  
6) Transport of residual waste in landfills; 
7) Transport of the Secondary raw materials (SRMs) produced by the recycling plant to the final use; 
8) Output of C&amp;D waste that goes to landfill (Process: Mixed C&amp;D waste, landfill); 
9) Output of ferrous metals that goes to sorting (Process: Metals, sorting). </common:generalComment>
      <referenceToExternalDocumentation type="source data set" refObjectId="070a5956-54e3-4831-85ee-691b74b177b9" version="01.00.000" uri="../sources/070a5956-54e3-4831-85ee-691b74b177b9.xml">
        <common:shortDescription>Carollo F. (2023). Circularity in construction and demolition waste management chain, Ph.D. Dissertation (Tutored by Rigamonti L., Ceruti F.). Politecnico di Milano. Background datasets from the EcoInvent database cut-off (v. 3.8) were used for the LCA study. </common:shortDescription>
      </referenceToExternalDocumentation>
    </dataSetInformation>
    <quantitativeReference type="Reference flow(s)">
      <referenceToReferenceFlow>0</referenceToReferenceFlow>
    </quantitativeReference>
